course: dictionary
lesson: 14805
title: Purchaser means buyer
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words ending in -er name the person who does something. A teacher teaches, a writer writes, and a purchaser buys things. «The purchaser paid for the bike at the till.» Who paid? The person who bought the bike, so a purchaser is a buyer.
explain: Purchaser is a formal word, so you will meet it more in adverts, contracts and maths problems than in everyday chat. «The purchaser pays for delivery.» The sentence tells you who must pay. Try swapping in buyer: «The buyer pays for delivery» still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
explain: In a maths problem, the purchaser is the person spending the money. «The purchaser bought three pens at 2 pounds each.» Work out 3 times 2 to find what was spent, then take that from the money given to find the change.
fact: A purchaser is a person or company that buys something.
fact: Purchaser means the same as buyer, but it is more formal.
fact: Purchaser is a noun, so you can write «a purchaser» or «purchasers».
fact: Phrases you may see are «the purchaser» and «a first-time purchaser», which means someone buying for the very first time.
fact: A company can be a purchaser too: «The school is the purchaser of the new computers.»
exercise: «The purchaser paid for the bike at the till.» What is a purchaser? | A bill sent after the sale | A person who sells things | A shop that is closed | *A person or company that buys something
exercise: «A first-time purchaser gets ten pounds off.» What does first-time purchaser mean? | A new sign on a shop | Someone who has bought something many times before | *Someone buying for the very first time | Someone who sells their first car
exercise: «Dev is the purchaser. He buys 3 pens at 2 pounds each.» Which word means the same as purchaser? | Shopkeeper | Seller | Owner | *Buyer
test: Which word means the same as purchaser? | Donor | Maker | Teacher | *Buyer
test: «The purchaser pays for delivery.» Who pays for delivery? | The factory | *The person buying | The delivery driver | The shop
exam: Maths: «A purchaser buys 4 apples at 3 pence each and pays with 20 pence.» How much change does the purchaser get? | 4 pence | 16 pence | *8 pence | 12 pence
